<title>FRANCE: JP Morgan fund to sell Valeo stake in 3-5 yrs. [CORRECTED 13:10 GMT]</title>
<headline>JP Morgan fund to sell Valeo stake in 3-5 yrs. [CORRECTED 13:10 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. fund JP Morgan GT Corporation (corrects headline and text from &quot;investment bank JP Morgan&quot;) said the 3.63 percent stake it is buying in French car parts maker Valeo from Cerus will be sold again in three to five years.</p>
<p>&quot;We take the equity for a while with the purpose of selling it again,&quot; said a JP Morgan spokeswoman in Paris. &quot;We agreed to sell in three to five years,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Asked by Reuters, she said there was no agreement to sell those shares to CGIP, the holding company which is buying 20.26 percent of Valeo to become its primary shareholder.</p>
</text>
